I recently decided to play a proper caveman (cavedwarf, actually), but
that plan went out the window when I came across a bones pile at
Delphi.  I was rather paniced when a 'C' with a /sleep decided to wield
Magicbane.  A bit of grafiti later, followed by some clubbing, an I was
the proud new owner of a rather ungrateful athame.

That isn't really where this story begins (or ends, for that matter ...
it's ongoing).  Over the course of the game I've found myself slinging
worthless glass about when I need a ranged weapon.  While not the best
option (skilled highly enchanted arrows are much better), it was a
suprisingly effective way of offing things like mindflayers.

And some other musings ...

When trying a to ascend a really goofy set of conducts (like everything
but wishless) ... "You disturbed me fool!" is not the correct answer
from a Dlvl.01 blessed magic lamp on turn 22.

If you're going to do a stupid ascension trick that involves hauling a
bunch of junk up to astral, an elf is probably not the best race to try
it with.

For reasons that make no sense whatsoever, I found myself doing a
little happy dance when Sunsword was generated in the Castle armoury
during a recent game.

It's amazing how little it takes to make someone go "Woot!" during a
wishless game.

It's probably a good idea to do every conduct separately before
attempting to combine them.

